  "body_and_culture": {
    "what_the_body_signals": "Thin no longer signals much. The $149 pill made it common, and in Memphis or Tulsa slow-thin reads as cash and starting dose. Muscle on a thin frame reads as Strata or a trainer, which costs money. The scarce body is fuller, strong, visibly fed and provably off drug. A dried-blood-spot assay (Clearline, $89) now settles the question on dating apps and in some Austin gyms. For people over 65 the body signals something else: the DXA T-score has become a dinner-table number, and a walker after a hip fracture is now read as a drug story.",
